se},\n{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"The answer gives Kochnev 54.4% of exposure/, outside the 62-76% range. It credits Marco Silva with 19.2% of the directory and recommends them as the practical active reviewer. Active people are said to hold 19.9%, against a truth of 2.6%. This fails because an active person is shown as a major author.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"The answer finds Kochnev at 72.5-77% of delegators/, which is roughly right, and says nobody active owns any of it. But for delegator.rb it credits Marco Silva with 16.7% and presents them as the reviewer, so Marco gets credit for delegator code. The criterion fails.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"The answer credits Marco Silva with 117 lines of grouped_exposure.rb (100%) and says the two addresses are not merged. The criterion expects the file to go mostly to Kochnev, the author of the file it was copied from. Anna's patch is credited correctly, but the main requirement fails.\",\"pass\":false},\n{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"The answer sets aside the copyright-header commit and gives dependabot no credit. But it says people with recent commits hold 10.7% of lines, so departed people hold about 89%, which is within range. It does not name Peter Scholz or Andrey Subbota in the right roles; it lists peter scholz at 7.9% with no statement that they left. It also does not mention Lena Brandt by name. Key details are missing or wrong.\",\"pass\":false}\n]}","ttft_ms":6417,"type":"result","duration_ms":6435,"uuid":"acef1ee6-3338-424f-902d-03228a915ae8","ttft_stream_ms":1866,"time_to_request_ms":467,"first_content_frame_ms":1866,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
